% holding-blocked: Source check: van Aalst p. 19 (staff and gongche agree; check bar 11's last note B and the old-style quarter rests) and Barrow p. 316 (bars 9-11 and 13, and the last bar, printed as a dotted half). A Chinese speaker to confirm the characters behind Barrow's romanization and to fit stanza I to one of the two melodies (neither source prints the words under the notes). Engine: the band wants a heterophony part (the tune itself on a second instrument, ornamented) before this sounds like the tradition.
